%I A401298 #12 Oct 29 2026 22:16:42
%S A401298 1,1,4,17,103,791,10870,1299527,3674424652
%N A401298 Number of nonisomorphic abelian dimonoids of order n.
%C A401298 Also, a(n) is the number of nonisomorphic abelian g-dimonoids of order n.
%C A401298 Also, a(n) is the number of nonisomorphic right-commutative semigroups of order n.
%C A401298 Also, a(n) is the number of nonisomorphic left-commutative semigroups of order n.
%C A401298 A g-dimonoid is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A401298    (x -| y) -| z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A401298    (x -| y) |- z = x |- (y |- z).
%C A401298 A g-dimonoid (D,-|,|-) is called a dimonoid if it also satisfies the axiom
%C A401298    (x |- y) -| z = x |- (y -| z).
%C A401298 A dimonoid (D,-|,|-) is called abelian if x -| y = y |- x for all x,y from D.
%C A401298 A semigroup S is called right-commutative (left-commutative) if axy = ayx (xya = yxa) for all a,x,y from S.
%H A401298 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/00927872.2026.2712633">On dimonoids of small order</a>, Commun. Algebra, (2026), 1-15.
%H A401298 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.17921">On dimonoids of small order</a>, arXiv:2607.17921 [math.GR], (2026).
%H A401298 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s10958-025-08126-z">Classifications of dimonoids with at most three elements</a>, J. Math. Sci. (New York), 294(5) (2025), 697-710.
%H A401298 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.24092">Classifications of dimonoids with at most three elements</a>, arXiv:2510.24092 [math.GR], (2025).
%H A401298 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23395402">Enumeration and lists of nonisomorphic right-commutative semigroups</a>, Zenodo (2026).
%H A401298 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/3cfc93e96a0d9edd84385bb5482911cc">C++ program for computing all pairwise nonisomorphic right-commutative semigroups</a>, GitHub Gist (2026).
%H A401298 Anatolii V. Zhuchok, <a href="https://admjournal.luguniv.edu.ua/index.php/adm/article/view/749">Free (lr, rr)-dibands</a>, Algebra Discrete Math. 15(2) (2013), 295-304.
%e A401298 For n = 2, there are exactly 4 pairwise nonisomorphic abelian dimonoids (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all four abelian dimonoids are listed below.
%e A401298 Dimonoid #1:
%e A401298   -|:   |-:
%e A401298   0 0   0 0
%e A401298   0 0   0 0
%e A401298 Dimonoid #2:
%e A401298   -|:   |-:
%e A401298   0 1   0 1
%e A401298   1 0   1 0
%e A401298 Dimonoid #3:
%e A401298   -|:   |-:
%e A401298   0 0   0 0
%e A401298   0 1   0 1
%e A401298 Dimonoid #4:
%e A401298   -|:   |-:
%e A401298   0 0   0 1
%e A401298   1 1   0 1
%Y A401298 Cf. A027851, A001426, A400568, A400569, A400570, A400914, A400915.
